---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { publicationAllows, publicationDecision } from '../lib/participation-publication-decision.mjs';
const base = '/participation-state-age-scenarios/20261107-01/';
type Range = { lower: number; upper: number } | null;
type Estimate = { state_code: string; contest_code: string; subset: number; prior_choice: string;
	birth_year_only_hypothetical_original_cohort: Range; estimated_current_reported_prior_count: number;
	reported_opposite_choice_count: number | null; birth_year_only_apparent_absence: Range;
	marginal_sensitivity_apparent_absence_count: Range;
	historical_certain_group_raw_n: number; historical_certain_group_effective_n: number };
type Coverage = { state_code: string; qualified_current_age_tables_in_frozen_release: number;
	released_state_contest_age_tables: number; status: string };
const review: { estimates: Estimate[]; jurisdiction_coverage: Coverage[] } =
	JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}summary.json`, 'utf8'));
const states: Record<string, string> = {
	CA: 'California', FL: 'Florida', IL: 'Illinois', MI: 'Michigan', NY: 'New York', TX: 'Texas' };
const count = (value: number | null) => value === null ? 'Unavailable'
	: (Math.round(value / 1000) * 1000).toLocaleString('en-US');
const range = (value: Range) => value === null ? 'Unavailable' : `${count(value.lower)} to ${count(value.upper)}`;
const coverageLabel = (value: string) => value === 'conditional_selected65plus_scenarios'
	? 'Reviewed age-65+ inputs; population results withheld' : value === 'withheld_historical_precision_disclosure'
		? 'Historical cohort not qualified for release' : 'No qualified current age comparison';
const publishAgeScaledScalars = publicationAllows(
	publicationDecision, 'age_scaled_original_coalition_counts_rates');
---

<section id="participation-state-age-scenarios" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="state-age-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">Conditional state scenarios · prospective age 65+</p>
		<h2 id="state-age-title">State age support and withheld cohort estimates</h2>
		<p>Six states, eight separate governor or Senate comparisons. Each uses its own state's
			2024 Harris or Trump coalition and CES birth-year composition, matched to that state's
			SSRS age-65+ population and joint-choice table and UF preliminary 2026 ballot estimate.
			No national estimate is allocated to states, counties or precincts.</p>
	</header>
	<p><strong>These are conditional scenarios, not measured staying home or turnout rates.</strong>
		The original cohort is hypothetically aged into 2026, not a linked panel of surviving
		residents. Apparent absence includes death, migration, recall and population/composition
		error. Survival is especially consequential for older cohorts. Negative residuals remain
		source/model diagnostics, not physical nonvoting counts.</p>
	{!publishAgeScaledScalars && <p data-publication-decision="historical-scalars-withheld"><strong>Historical evidence decision:</strong>
		state age-scaled original-coalition, switching and apparent-absence quantities are withheld. Historical
		support diagnostics and 51-jurisdiction coverage remain below.</p>}
	{publishAgeScaledScalars && <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="State age-65+ conditional reference scenarios">
		<table>
			<caption>All rows concern prospective age 65+. Counts rounded to the nearest thousand.
				Birthday-only ranges are not sampling, survival or total uncertainty intervals.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">2026 contest</th><th scope="col">Reported switch</th>
				<th scope="col">Hypothetical original coalition</th><th scope="col">Current reported prior voters</th>
				<th scope="col">Reported opposite choice</th><th scope="col">Apparent absence: birthday-only</th>
				<th scope="col">Apparent absence: assumed stress</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>{review.estimates.map(row => <tr data-state-age-coalition={`${row.state_code}-${row.contest_code}-${row.prior_choice}`}>
				<th scope="row">{states[row.state_code]}</th><td>{row.contest_code === 'GG' ? 'Governor' : 'Senate'}</td>
				<td>{row.prior_choice === 'D' ? 'Harris to R' : 'Trump to D'}</td>
				<td>{range(row.birth_year_only_hypothetical_original_cohort)}</td>
				<td>{count(row.estimated_current_reported_prior_count)}</td>
				<td data-state-age-switchers>{count(row.reported_opposite_choice_count)}</td>
				<td data-state-age-absence>{range(row.birth_year_only_apparent_absence)}</td>
				<td data-state-age-stress>{range(row.marginal_sensitivity_apparent_absence_count)}</td>
			</tr>)}</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>}
	{publishAgeScaledScalars && <p><strong>No design confidence intervals are available.</strong> The 486 scenarios per row
		vary birthday endpoints, assumed historical composition by -2/0/+2 percentage points,
		preliminary ballots by 95/100/105%, group/prior rounding by -0.5/0/+0.5 points and balanced
		recalled-choice transfers by -2/0/+2 points. These stresses do not empirically cover
		historical state sampling error or current joint-cell uncertainty. Conditional choice is
		held fixed; a separate rounding envelope is in the download. Offices and marginal endpoints
		are not additive.</p>}
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Historical support, source matching and withheld estimates</summary>
		<p>A conservative historical-support screen informed the review, but is not a precision
			guarantee or automatic publication rule. State-specific weights, validated 2024 turnout,
			presidential choice, prospective age, current population matching and disclosure were
			reviewed separately. Younger and smaller groups are not promoted to precise estimates.
			Historical and current outcome calibration are not independent validation.</p>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="State historical age support diagnostics">
			<table>
				<caption>Certain-age historical support only; raw and effective n do not supply joint-cell design precision.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">State / contest</th><th scope="col">Prior vote</th>
					<th scope="col">Historical raw n</th><th scope="col">Historical effective n</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{review.estimates.map(row => <tr data-state-age-support>
					<th scope="row">{states[row.state_code]} / {row.contest_code === 'GG' ? 'Governor' : 'Senate'}</th>
					<td>{row.prior_choice === 'D' ? 'Harris' : 'Trump'}</td>
					<td>{row.historical_certain_group_raw_n.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
					<td>{row.historical_certain_group_effective_n.toFixed(1)}</td>
				</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p>SSRS can retain pre-election intentions. The calculation assumes the published group
			and prior-choice composition applies to all matching estimated ballot-casters; exact
			response selection remains unresolved. Unknown birthdays are not imputed. Source
			suppression stays unavailable. No current electorate is reweighted to the 2024 partisan split.</p>
		<p>Measured staying home, identified new/returning voters, demographic turnout, causal
			persuasion and shares of total swing remain unavailable. This package contains complete
			permitted selected inputs, methods, code/tests and all 7,776 scenarios, not personal
			records, small birthday-boundary cells or restricted NORC materials.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>All 50 states and D.C.: release coverage</summary>
		<p>Six states have archived conditional inputs, not currently released population estimates.
			Missing observations are not zero turnout. The complete download also records
			all 54 matched current age tables not qualified for this historical-cohort release.</p>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All-jurisdiction state age scenario coverage">
			<table>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Jurisdiction</th><th scope="col">Matched current age tables</th>
					<th scope="col">Archived contest-age tables</th><th scope="col">Current status</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{review.jurisdiction_coverage.map(row => <tr data-state-age-coverage={row.state_code}>
					<th scope="row">{row.state_code}</th><td>{row.qualified_current_age_tables_in_frozen_release}</td>
					<td>{row.released_state_contest_age_tables}</td><td>{coverageLabel(row.status)}</td>
				</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete archived state-age inputs + code + results (ZIP; unsupported population scalars)</a>
		<a href={`${base}summary.json`} download>Archived state-age summary + coverage (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>State-age archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-state-age-scenarios { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
</style>
